comments[6]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-07T09:04:00.674Z","harness:claude-code","Implementation evidence (branch feat/extension-authoring-contracts, 2026-11-07).\n\nRoot cause: the definition-driven extension option grammar lived in src/cli and ran only on CLI argv dispatch. The SDK path (dispatchActiveExtensionAction in src/sdk/runtime.ts, reached by PmClient.run and MCP) and runRegisteredCommandForTest passed options through raw, so a CLI spelling such as status-filter never reached the handler key statusFilter and the declared default applied instead.\n\nChange:\n- Moved the module to src/sdk/extension/command-options.ts so the SDK can share it (no sdk -> cli import exists anywhere).\n- New normalizeDirectExtensionCommandOptions folds each declared spelling (statusFilter, status-filter, --status-filter, short letter) into the handler key, treats undefined as omitted, refuses two spellings with different values (extension_option_spelling_conflict, exit 2, names both keys and the handler key), then runs the same coerceLooseCommandOptionsWithFlagDefinitions as CLI dispatch (defaults, coercion, strict validation). Undeclared keys pass through unchanged for SDK compatibility.\n- PmClient.run/MCP dispatch and the harness both call it; the harness finds the declared flags through a WeakMap keyed by activation.commands, so existing package tests need no new argument. A hand-built registry passes options through verbatim.\n- pm contracts --command <cmd> --flags-only --json publishes sdk_option and owner extension on every extension row; help --json options carry the same fields.\n- MCP tool-schema property names now use the same handler key (only changes legacy underscore flags such as --include_history, whose old property includehistory never reached the handler).\n- collectExtensionFlagDefinitionsForCommand moved beside it and is shared by CLI and SDK.\n\nBehavior change for direct callers (migration line): PmClient.run, MCP and the test harness now apply declared defaults and value coercion for extension flags exactly as the CLI does, so a handler that echoes options sees the default keys and booleans instead of raw strings.\n\nVerified: tests/integration/extensions/extension-option-contract.integration.spec.ts (CLI argv, PmClient.run with three spellings, harness, conflict refusal) and tests/unit/sdk/extension-command-options.spec.ts pass. Negative control: replacing the SDK normalizer with identity makes the integration spec fail with selection undefined instead of closed.\n"
  "2026-11-07T10:00:01.498Z","harness:claude-code","Codex review round 1 (gpt-6.1-sol, xhigh, local, uncommitted diff) found four defects, all fixed with regressions:\n- P1: a strict boolean switch passed directly (PmClient.run, MCP or the harness) as \"nonsense\" became true, because the CLI coercer treats a separated token after a switch as a positional. Direct values are now recorded as attached occurrences (like --commit=value), so the existing attached-switch check refuses them with extension_flag_value_invalid; arrays become one occurrence per entry. Regression in tests/unit/sdk/extension/command-options.spec.ts; negative control (passing the folded options without recorded occurrences) fails it.\n- P2: the root-only refusal ran only for commands that declare flags. It moved into refuseUndeclaredRootOnlyOptions, called from the extension action wrapper for every extension command; the integration spec now covers demo-plain (no flags) with --all and --explain (code unknown_option).\n- P2: the signature gate skipped callable variable exports (runUpdateMany, resolveContentFieldFilters). It now checks every exported function and every exported variable annotation (checked_values in the snapshot); eight more gaps closed (UpdateManyCommandOptions, UpdateManyResult, ContentFieldFilters, MissingMetadataFilters, BuiltinItemType, GovernanceStartBlockerEnforcement).\n- P2: inline import(\"./x.js\").T references bypassed the visitor. ImportTypeNode qualifiers now resolve like ordinary references; typeof import(...) names no type.\n"
  "2026-11-07T10:13:06.743Z","harness:claude-code","Codex review round 2 (gpt-6.1-sol, xhigh) confirmed the round 1 fixes and found four more defects, all fixed with regressions:\n- P1: the root-only refusal also ran on core commands that an extension only augments with flags (pm-command-kit adds flags to list, so pm list --all failed with unknown_option). It now runs only for extension-created command nodes (isExtensionCreatedCommand); the integration spec registers a flag on list and asserts pm list --all --demo-extra keeps status all.\n- P2: nested list values passed directly ([[true, \"false\"]]) were validated as scalars before flattening. Direct occurrences now flatten recursively, matching the list coercer.\n- P2 (gate): typeof HiddenClass (a TypeQuery) bypassed the census. Type queries now resolve; a query of a package value (typeof internalRun) follows that value's own signature, with a cycle guard. Following it exposed two real gaps (PmSettings for sdk/merge resolveProjectMergeTypeFolders, LoadedRuntimeSchemaSections for loadGuardedRuntimeSchema), now re-exported.\n- P2 (gate): enum member references (State.Ready) now resolve to the declaring enum.\nTest seams: following type queries also reached the _testOnly* exports (internal functions exposed for pm's own tests). These are exempt by naming convention and counted as exempt_test_seams per entrypoint in the snapshot, so publishing internal test-seam types never becomes a requirement.\n"
  "2026-11-07T10:28:22.424Z","harness:claude-code","Codex review round 3 (gpt-6.1-sol, xhigh) found three P2 defects, all fixed with regressions:\n- Direct short aliases were folded case-insensitively, so with --small/-s and --sort-order/-S a direct { S } reached small and { s, S } raised a false spelling conflict. Short letters are now indexed case-sensitively (Commander keeps -s and -S distinct on the CLI); long spellings still fold through the camel-case key.\n- On a core command an extension augments (provider mixed, for example an extension flag on list), extension rows carried no owner or sdk_option. Extension-contributed rows are now decorated on every command; inherited_flags stays limited to extension-provided commands. The integration spec asserts the mixed list entry.\n- The signature gate ignored type queries of methods and callable properties (typeof api.run). publicSignatureNodes now covers every function-like declaration and property annotations; the real SDK has no new gaps.\n"
  "2026-11-07T10:39:47.446Z","harness:claude-code","Codex review round 4 (gpt-6.1-sol, xhigh) found three P2 items:\n- Fixed: the shared coercer folded a lower-cased short alias into another flag's own key, so with --sort-order/-S and an independent --s, { s: \"lower\", sortOrder: \"upper\" } lost s (on direct calls and on CLI argv dispatch alike). coerceLooseCommandOptionsWithFlagDefinitions now drops alias spellings that are another declaration's canonical key; regressions cover both the direct normalizer and the coercer.\n- Fixed: typeof HiddenClass.prototype resolved to the synthetic prototype symbol and bypassed the gate; the owning class is now resolved like an enum member.\n- Deferred to pm-bqyk1z with the repro: a callable value annotated with an exported alias (type Runner = (o: Hidden) => void) whose own parameter type is unexported. That is the transitive type-declaration closure pm-bqyk1z owns.\nConvergence note: rounds found 4, 4, 3, 3 items, each round a narrower declaration form or alias composition; the remaining class is the closure work already scoped in pm-bqyk1z.\n"
  "2026-11-07T12:24:41.449Z","harness:claude-code","Greptile review on PR 1682 (P2, fixed): an undeclared direct key equal to a lower-cased short alias (s beside --sort-order/-S) was still rewritten or absorbed by the coercer's CLI alias folding. normalizeDirectExtensionCommandOptions now passes only the folded handler keys to the shared coercer and returns undeclared keys untouched; regression in tests/unit/sdk/extension/command-options.spec.ts."
